  "title": "Hwaseong Fortress",
  "summary": "Hwaseong Fortress in Suwon was built between 1794 and 1796 under King Jeongjo, in about two and a half years. Its rampart is 5.7 km long, averaging 5 m in height, with four main gates. Jeong Yak-yong is credited with leading its construction, and it was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List in 1997.",
